SAFETY-NETTING ESCALATION PLAN

Immediate presentation to the Emergency Department or call 000 if developing a sudden, fixed heart rate over 150 bpm that does not change with resting, sudden crushing central chest pain radiating to the jaw, complete loss of consciousness (fainting), audible high-pitched wheezing from the throat (stridor), or a sudden inability to swallow saliva.

